92186149955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421791 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186149955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421799 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186149955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421811 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186149955 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421791 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186151984 1071 "Consider the differential equation $y'' - 3y'+ 2y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y_1(x) = e^{x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- $y_2(x) = e^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n\n- The general solution of the equation is $y=Ae^{x} + Be^{2x}.$" 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186151984 1071 "Consider the differential equation $y'' - 3y'+ 2y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $y_1(x) = e^{x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n\nII. $y_2(x) = e^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n\nIII. The general solution of the equation is $y=Ae^{x} + Be^{2x}.$" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152291 1038 #edb/ref 17592186421820 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152291 1038 #edb/ref 17592186421821 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152292 1038 #edb/ref 17592186421822 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152293 1038 #edb/ref 17592186421819 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152359 1050 1140.0 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152577 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152577 1071 "$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-15y=-7{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-3x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{4x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{4x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186152577 1071 "$y^{″} - 2y^{′} - 15y =-7e^{4x}$\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is $y_{c}(x) = Ae^{5x} + Be^{-3x}$, where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.\nThe function $y_{p}(x) = e^{4x}$\n{{field-1}}\na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nThe function $y_{p}(x) = xe^{4x}$\n{{field-2}}\na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$y(x) =$\n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\nwhere\n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186152577 1074 "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{4x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{4x})^{′}=4{e}^{4x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(4{e}^{4x})^{′}=16{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(16{e}^{4x})-2(4{e}^{4x})-15({e}^{4x})=-7{e}^{4x}.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{4x}$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{4x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x{e}^{4x})^{′}={e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =({e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x})^{′}=8{e}^{4x}+16x{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(8{e}^{4x}+16x{e}^{4x})-2({e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x})-15(x{e}^{4x})=-7{e}^{4x}.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{4x}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-3x}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-3x}+{e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants." 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186314139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313381 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186314139 1078 #edb/ref 17592186313381 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186314139 1078 #edb/ref 17592186313491 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186314340 1075 #edb/ref 17592186312580 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186314340 1078 #edb/ref 17592186312580 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186314340 1078 #edb/ref 17592186313155 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186314656 1075 #edb/ref 17592186313947 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186314656 1078 #edb/ref 17592186312621 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186314656 1078 #edb/ref 17592186313947 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186314878 1071 "$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+4y=3{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186314878 1071 "$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+4y=3{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-4x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{-x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." 13194139534443 17592186045417 false] [17592186421786 1080 "I, II, and III" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421786 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421786 1083 #uuid "0246f7ce-f1b2-5e93-8e63-e7393dc569b3" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421787 1080 "y=A{x}^{-2}+B{x}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421787 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421787 1083 #uuid "05fa078e-be12-5c3b-bea0-316dbe5fdadb" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421788 1080 "y=A{x}^{-2}+B{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421788 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421788 1083 #uuid "07ce657b-e482-5f99-bc7d-7195f7a26f4d" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421789 1080 "A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{3x}" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421789 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421789 1083 #uuid "10f3beec-4202-5dab-a3d5-826a80ea36b3" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421790 1080 "{e}^{4x}" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421790 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421790 1083 #uuid "201d8ac2-9e51-5cf5-98c1-c1ef06a0df77" 13194139534443 17592186045417 true] [17592186421791 1080 "A{e}^{5x}